  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 01f934d50526431a9392a6ceca1dc33d, type: 3}
  m_Name: Rampage Cell Config 3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  CellName: Rampage
  Description: Demolition arena cell, intensity 3 of 4 - a busy arena: 137 seeded plants totalling
    ~22820 prisms of cacti, spires, pines, rosettes and coral, filling the volume from just
    outside the nucleus out to the membrane, across all three domains, each plant one of the
    four elemental variations. Intensity 4 is the shipped, play-tested arena EXACTLY; 1 is
    that same arena made bigger, denser and easier to hit: 2.33x the plant count, prisms at
    1.2x the authored leaf (bigger is an easier target for the cone and an easier surface to
    skim), a nucleus at prefab scale 300 (~294u radius), 3x the authored wildlife, and -
    authored in the scene, not here - one crystal fewer than players. The nucleus stays
    clear (the planting band is clamped outside it) and is the crystals' contested ground.
    The mature forest is ~1,559,724 volume, and this cell's VOLUME thresholds are the
    play-tested intensity-4 ladder scaled by that - so Frenzy sits the same 4.11x above the
    forest at every level. Collider envelope: up to 23,250 prisms (LOD-cullable, and the
    count backstop freezes growth there) plus 205 always-on heart-crystal colliders at the
    plant cap. Pending an in-editor re-measure; regenerate with
    Tools/Build/rampage_intensity.py rather than hand-editing.
